  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.16\n- Fixed RegisterAsync throwing ArgumentNullException when called without RegisterOptions. Registration with a null options now uses the configured MessagingBlazorOptions.VapidKey as documented (null = defaults), instead of crashing. Added regression tests covering the null-options and explicit-VAPID-key paths.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.15\n- Fixed ServiceWorkerPath and ServiceWorkerScope being ignored. The page JS module now accepts (path, scope), and the interop/lifecycle coordinator forward the configured values to navigator.serviceWorker.register. Consuming apps can now point registration at the package's shipped service worker (e.g. /_content/FireForNet.Firebase.Messaging.Blazor/fireForNet-messaging-sw.js) without vendoring a copy into their own wwwroot.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.14\n- Initial Blazor Firebase Messaging integration: FID-based registration, foreground/notification event relay, permission management, config-free service worker, capability detection.\n- Uses IFirebaseInstallations directly for the FIS auth token and persistent FID.",
